      "message": "\u003e Now that you have moved period calculation to the upper if block, phase calculation can be simplified too:\n\u003e \n\u003e 1. Change time from int8_t to uint8_t\n \u003e\u003e Ack.\n\n\u003e 2. Change LED_INDEFINITE to be UINT8_MAX instead of -1\n\u003e 3. Here you can do this all the time without the comparison to LED_INDEFINITE:\n\u003e phase \u003d ticks \u003c led_state_table[led_state][LED_PHASE_0].time ? 0 : 1;\n\u003e ticks \u003d (ticks + 1) % period;\n\u003e 4. Changing LED_INDEFINITE to UINT8_MAX will also mean that period is set to UINT8_MAX when phase 0 is defined as indefinite in L158.\n\n  \u003e\u003e Wont we want to use the chance to avoid calculating (add / modulo etc) when its LED_INDEFINITE for phase 0 and let it continue until there is a state change.\n\n\u003e 5. Also, you don\u0027t need to initialize period to UINT8_MAX any more in L147.\n\u003e\u003e Ack.",
